A command with two init functions, which share one reference. The first holds a
type error, the second a dead store, so the second's store is reported: the type
error skips the first init alone.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

func init() {
	println(undefinedName)
}

func init() {
	v := 1
	v = 2
	_ = v
}
